            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Running a successful freight trucking business takes more than grit and good drivers. It takes reliable equipment, strategic investment, and a partner that understands your goals.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Whether you’re a solo operator or managing a growing fleet, your trucks are the backbone of your business. Upgrading to new equipment can feel like a big decision, but it often comes with even bigger rewards. Let’s explore how adding a <a href=\"/store/inventory?condition=new\">new semi truck</a> to your operation can support growth, increase reliability, and help you scale smarter, not harder.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-landscape",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Freight Trucking Landscape Today",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "landscape"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-landscape-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Freight trucking is a highly competitive industry, especially in Florida, where demand is high and timelines are tight. Delays, maintenance issues, and inconsistent equipment can make or break your ability to win contracts and retain customers. Beyond that, here are some other reasons why up-to-date equipment matters:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-landscape-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Customer expectations are rising for on-time, trackable deliveries"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Shippers prefer fleets that operate newer, more reliable trucks"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Drivers are harder to recruit without modern, comfortable cabs"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-landscape-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<a href=\"/financing\">Investing in new trucks</a> doesn’t just improve how your business runs today; it positions you for long-term success tomorrow.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-growth",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How a New Semi Truck Supports Business Growth",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "growth"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-growth-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every hour your truck is on the road is an opportunity to move freight, make money, and build your reputation. Here’s how a <a href=\"/store/inventory?condition=new\">new truck</a> helps boost your capacity and performance.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "features-growth-2",
                  "type": "list",
                  "props": {
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "columns": 2,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Improved Uptime",
                        "desc": "Newer trucks experience fewer breakdowns and require fewer frequent repairs. This means more time hauling loads and less time in the shop."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Better Fuel Efficiency",
                        "desc": "Modern semi trucks are designed with fuel economy in mind. Over time, these savings add up and improve your margins, especially when fuel prices spike."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Enhanced Safety & Compliance",
                        "desc": "Features like lane assist, adaptive cruise control, and real-time diagnostics not only protect your drivers but also help you stay compliant with DOT regulations."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Stronger Brand Reputation",
                        "desc": "Shippers and brokers take notice of fleets that invest in new, clean, and professional-looking equipment. It reflects well on your business and builds trust."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-growth-3-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-growth-3",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
